<title>UK: Baltic Freight Index rose three points to 1,291.</title>
<headline>Baltic Freight Index rose three points to 1,291.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Baltic Freight Index for spot dry cargo shipping rates rose to 1,291 today from 1,288 on May 21, with the base being Jan 4 1985 equals 1,000. The BFI is based on the following sub-indices with rates in dollars per tonne.</p>
<p> Route Index     Rate   Prev Index  Rate</p>
<p>   1    1350    12.256	  1350    12.256</p>
<p>   1a   1297  9825.000	  1296  9819.000</p>
<p>   2    1536    21.950	  1533    21.894</p>
<p>   2a   1504 12331.000	  1510 12381.000</p>
<p>   3    1368    12.625	  1372    12.656</p>
<p>   3a   1220  9631.000	  1216  9594.000</p>
<p>   6    1221    12.594	  1218    12.563</p>
<p>   7    1175     5.719	  1166     5.675</p>
<p>   8     862     9.481	   862     9.481</p>
<p>   9     768  6719.000	   759  6641.000</p>
<p>  10    1122     5.669	  1116     5.638</p>
